exports[`aws.auth.demo.plan given: [case4] a caller whose creds and reach identity are found when: [t0] no .env and no shell pair then: it reads the pair off the live role, warns the principal is unchecked, and never applies 1`] = `
"🐢 reef check...

🐚 aws.auth.demo.plan
   ├─ caller: arn:aws:sts::000000000000:assumed-role/example.test.profile/session
   ├─ reach identity from: live role ehmpathy-demo-for-grove
   │  └─ ⚠️ principal NOT checked: read off the live role, so it cannot differ from it
   └─ plan into: provision/aws.auth/account=demo/.temp/plan.readonly.json

(declastruct plan output)

🐚 plan tally
   ├─ KEEP: 2
   └─ UPDATE: 1
      └─ DeclaredAwsIamRole.ehmpathy-demo-for-grove
         ├─ - "action": "sts:AssumeRole",
         ├─ + "action": Array [
         ├─ +   "sts:AssumeRole",
         ├─ +   "sts:TagSession",
         ├─ +   "sts:SetSourceIdentity",
         └─ + ],

🐢 plan written. read it before any apply; this skill never applies

🐚 before any apply
   ├─ ⚠️ principal NOT checked; the applier's own plan, from the applier's .env, owns that check
   └─ to apply: the applier's own shell, per account=demo/readme.md (admin creds + .env, plan, apply)
"
`;

